    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Seen in behavioral health consultation at the request of Elena Marquez, MD. [S]</paragraph><list><item>Trauma-related symptoms interfere with sleep, mood, and sense of safety. [S]</item></list><paragraph>Historical basis. These claims are historical evidence, not findings from a modern examination.</paragraph><list><item>Audie Leon Murphy was born June 20, 1924. [D]</item><item>Murphy served in World War II and became one of the most decorated United States soldiers of the war. [D]</item><item>Murphy was wounded in the leg during the January 26, 1945 action near Holtzwihr and was wounded three times during the war. [D]</item><item>Murphy experienced postwar nightmares and insomnia. [D]</item><item>Murphy experienced postwar depression and headaches. [D]</item><item>Murphy&apos;s postwar symptoms are retrospectively described as post-traumatic stress disorder. [R]</item><item>Murphy reported sleeping with a loaded pistol under his pillow. [D]</item></list><paragraph>1 later historical claim is omitted because it describes events after the index age. See the teaching note.</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

